# Vertical List

The simplest setup — a single `DndDroppable` with `direction="vertical"` (the default).

This example uses 50 items to demonstrate **auto-scroll** near the container edges. Use the **Scroll config** panel to tune auto-scroll behaviour in real time via `controller.setScrollConfig()`:

- **Scroll zone ratio** — how close to the edge (as a fraction of container height) the cursor must be to trigger scrolling
- **Max speed** — maximum scroll speed in px/frame at 60 fps

```ts
// set once at creation
const controller = new DndController({ scrollZoneRatio: 0.2, maxSpeed: 15 });

// or update at any time
controller.setScrollConfig({ maxSpeed: 50 });
```

The `onDrop` callback receives the drop `position` — splice the source item out and insert it at the new position.

